    command "cargo test -p akr-mcp --test conformance; mcpprobe post|auto /home/dk/.local/bin/akr-mcp with PROBE_TOOL=knowledge.start"
    summary """
        Every tool result carried resultType 'tool', a value outside MCP's closed set (complete, input_required, task), so rmcp 3.x clients rejected the response itself and Codex 0.149 could call no knowledge tool at all. Now 'complete'. tests/conformance.rs asserts the envelope of all 23 tools plus the handshakes against written-out closed sets; reintroducing the bug fails 2 of its 4 tests. A real rmcp 3.1.2 client now completes knowledge.start on both lifecycles.
        """
}

record akr.evidence.warm-search-stays-git-free-after-changes/1 : evidence {
    title "a_current_index_search_does_not_invoke_git passed in a 10-test run of the akr-cli search suite. It builds the index, then runs akr search with PATH pointed at an empty directory, so a git subprocess could not be found if one were attempted; the command exits 0 and returns results. The fast path is structurally git-free rather than merely quick, and this pass's akr-cli and akr-mcp changes did not disturb it."
    state verified
    result pass
    method observation
    observed_at git:05fea30a52f59775917cf5a1d1ac1241c0392b44
    summary """
